From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0406-black-world-06-upscale-small-source-and-rt-trace.patch

Source: 0406-black-world-06-upscale-small-source-and-rt-trace.patch
ring (EDEN_NX2_UPSCALE_SOURCE_SIZE), EDEN_NX2_TRACE_RT

Runs 81-84 (T23, Handheld, Max Resolution) and run79-picture-stages.md: the clean world was a
960x540 B10G11R11 image stretched onto the network's 1920x1080 output (run82 line 6001); the
480x270 images showed limbs; the speckles were a 256x256 onto a 512x512. All came from the blind
cbuf0 scan reading two fixed words of the network's constant buffer, +0xa0 = 24576 and +0xb8 =
12288 (an address and a size), as TIC numbers: whenever the game's per-frame TIC ring had just
passed those numbers (+0xc0 stood at 24588, 24586, 12337 at the first pairs) they named a live
image and the picture changed. No resolution drop, no location.

EDEN_NX2_UPSCALE_SOURCE_SIZE=<width>x<height>, or "half": for a 1:1 network (own read and store
of one size), the copy's source is an image of that size in the output's format, looked for among
the game's own TIC entries within 256 of the network's input entry (its per-frame ring), the one
nearest that entry; kept per program and re-read every dispatch while it names the same image;
the own pair's copy when there is none. Such a program never takes the Bananza slots or the cbuf0
scan (EDEN_NX2_UPSCALE_HANDLES_ONLY is implied for it). The candidates found are logged on change:
"960x540 format 33 candidates near tic 24588: tic 24590 0x... tic 24601 0x...". Replaces the
EDEN_NX2_UPSCALE_QUARTER of the earlier black-world-06, which took 480x270 from the same two words.

Trace: with EDEN_NX2_UPSCALE_TRACE=1 a "source (<step>): <address> WxH format F tic N; own +0xc0
tic N <address>, out +0xd0 <address>" line, logged on each change with a cap of 64 per program,
separate from the size-only outcome line, so a same-size source change and the ring's position are
visible too.

EDEN_NX2_TRACE_RT=<width>x<height>[,...]: describes draws into render targets of these sizes like
the after-upscale trace (render target, vertex and pixel program, the fragment stage's sampled
images, blend), the first 48 of each size and then every 500th. Use 960x540,1920x1080: what writes
the 960x540 image and what it samples, and the 1920x1080 draws into the network's input memory
with their format code.

All unset: nothing changes. Clang syntax check, no warnings, after black-world-01..05. Not built,
not run.

